 {"id": "PEDS-U143", "ch": 17, "n": 6, "title": "Refractory Rickets — Treatment, VDDR and Approach Algorithm", "sec": "VDDR · p72", "qs": ["PEDS-C17-061", "PEDS-C17-062", "PEDS-C17-063", "PEDS-C17-064", "PEDS-C17-065", "PEDS-C17-066", "PEDS-C17-067", "PEDS-C17-068", "PEDS-C17-069", "PEDS-C17-070", "PEDS-C17-071", "PEDS-C17-072", "PEDS-C17-073", "PEDS-C17-074", "PEDS-C17-075"], "guide": "Familial hypophosphatemic Treatment 1. Phosphate supplementation Joule solution (elemental phosphates) 2. Burosumab newer drug monoclonal antibody against FGF-23. VDDR Autosomal recessive, Defects in Vit D metabolism → Hypocalcemia. Features Classic rickets + Type II additional Ectodermal defects (Milia, epidermal cysts), Oligodontia (↓ teeth), Alopecia. Treatment Type I α calcidiol (active form of Vit D) + Ca²⁺ supplements; Type II High doses Vit D → partially overcome resistance → improves symptoms. Approach (biochemical values) High PO₄³⁻ → CKD associated (↓ excretion PO₄³⁻); Low PO₄³⁻ → ABG Acidosis(+) → RTA; Acidosis(−) → PTH High (response to ↓Ca²⁺) → VDDR; Normal → Familial hypophosphatemic."},
